{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70b.md; rg -n '§0|\"'^#|''^0'\"\\\\.' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r70b.md; rg -n '§0|\"'^#|''^0'\"\\\\.' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\"","aggregated_output":"1. **One of the six cards still hides evidence.** The E “can’t tell yet” answer names 15 passages, but readers see only 9. Five of the six missing passages weigh against the forecast. The renderer skips `pushes[].evidence_id`. Including those IDs in memory restored all six passages and left the other five cards unchanged. Across all six cards, all 61 displayed figures matched the writer’s values and all recomputed outcomes stayed the same. S’s `F13` now correctly identifies $745B of capital expenditure. [E answer:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:84) · [paid_gate.py:579](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:579) · [S answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/S/answers/claude.json:1)\n\n2. **The renderer also adds an unrequested limit on passage ranges.** In a separate in-memory check using E’s actual passages, `e4687–e4764` returned only its endpoints and skipped three available passages. The code expands a range only when its endpoints differ by 50 or less. The registered rule requires every named passage. [paid_gate.py:496](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:496) · [PAID-GATE.md:256](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:256)\n\n3. **The reader instructions and packet delivery pass.** The brief carries D747 and D753 faithfully and names no case. The four questions, verdict thresholds and third-reader rule are unchanged. On a 27-packet rehearsal file, all three batches and the third-reader prompt carried the exact packet bytes, including the key commitment. The third reader also received both readings on the disputed question. [reader-brief-v13s.md:17](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/reader-brief-v13s.md:17) · [PAID-GATE.md:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:263) · [assemble_readings.py:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/assemble_readings.py:49)\n\n4. **The launch checks pass.** All 12 rebuilt requests matched the plan pin byte for byte, giving 36 first attempts under the $0.50 total cap. The v13s authorization and output folder were absent. The documented command uses the correct repository-root path and places the detached log and PID outside the run folder. This review spent $0. [Plan pin:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.sha256:1) · [paid_gate.py:431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:431) · [PAID-GATE.md:311](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:311)\n\n**Verdict — do not send.** Keep the one-time authorization unused until readers can see every passage the answer names.1:# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n12:## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n25:## 1. Goal (end to end)\n31:## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n57:## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n67:| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n70:## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n93:## 5. What to do\n120:## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n168:## 7. Process (no drift)\n179:## 8. Steps and where we are\n193:## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
