{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md'","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '1,125p;350,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py | sed -n '1,125p;350,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The paid gate of judging-v13 (D725's registered test; D729, D730). Harness-only; nothing here is product code.\n     2\t\n     3\t  python3 paid_gate.py plan <out.json>                        # $0: build every request from the stored runs and check them\n     4\t  python3 paid_gate.py send <new out folder> <ceiling>        # paid: only at the ceiling Alex names (APPROVED_CEILING)\n     5\t  python3 paid_gate.py packets <out folder> <key folder>      # $0: blind reading packets, the arm hidden; the key kept outside the repo\n     6\t  python3 paid_gate.py verdict <out folder> <readings.json> <key folder>   # $0: the registered pass and stop lines\n     7\t\n     8\tThe test (D725, RESULT.md): the 09-20 total and Data Center pair in each of three stored draws, judged jointly (one v13 family call)\n     9\tand separately (each member alone, the same union of evidence, the same v13 format), three samples each; plus three samples each of\n    10\tthe O, S and E singletons. 9 + 18 + 9 = 36 first attempts. A calculation the checks refuse is retried once with its errors; a second\n    11\trefusal makes the unit unresolved. The separate arm's two answers are then reconciled by the same checks over the pair's family.\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\timport hashlib\n    14\timport json\n    15\timport random\n    16\timport re\n    17\timport secrets\n    18\timport sqlite3\n    19\timport sys\n    20\timport threading\n    21\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    22\t\n    23\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    24\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    25\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    26\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    27\timport calc_check as cc                                                 # noqa: E402\n    28\timport calc_small as cs                                                 # noqa: E402\n    29\timport render_v13 as rv                                                 # noqa: E402\n    30\tfrom hivemind import config, model                                      # noqa: E402\n    31\t\n    32\tRUN = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    33\tCONFIG = REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'                              # its re-judging model setting: gpt-6-luna, medium, 16000 output tokens\n    34\tSYSTEM = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n    35\tSYSTEM_S = (HERE / 'judging-v13s.txt').read_text()                      # the small format (D737): one sentence changed\n    36\tCHECKERS = {None: cc, 'v13': cc, 'v13s': cs}\n    37\tAPPROVED_CEILING = 0.5                                                  # Alex, 2026-11-22 (D732): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"\n    38\tPINNED_PLAN_SHA256 = (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan.sha256').exists() else None\n    39\tAUTH = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/authorization.json'\n    40\t# D753: Alex's one-time exception, a v13s re-send. Its own reviewed plan pin and its own one-time authorization; the v13 ones stay.\n    41\tPINNED_PLAN_V13S = (HERE / 'paid-plan-v13s.sha256').read_text().strip() if (HERE / 'paid-plan-v13s.sha256').exists() else None\n    42\tAUTH_V13S = Path.home() / '.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json'\n    43\tDRAWS = (1, 2, 3)\n    44\tRETRY_MARK = '\\n\\nThe code refused the previous answer because: '\n    45\tPAIRS = [('old-1', ('v4', 9014), ('v8', 9022)), ('old-2', ('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)), ('old-3', ('v3', 9183), ('v35', 9177))]\n    46\tSINGLETONS = [('O', 'old-2', 'v29', 8734, ('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', 'company', 'end of FY2027')),\n    47\t              ('S', 'old-2', 'v6', 8595, ('four largest AI hyperscalers', 'data-center capex', 'combined', 'CY2027')),\n    48\t              ('E', 'old-3', 'v41', 9166, ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2028'))]\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    52\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef bands(draw, view_id):\n    56\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    57\t    rows = conn.execute('select lo, hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    58\t    return [[lo / 1e9 if lo is not None else None, hi / 1e9 if hi is not None else None] for lo, hi in rows]\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef passages(draw, evidence_ids):\n    62\t    \"\"\"What each request showed of a passage: the quote cut at 400 characters (judging._lines_english).\"\"\"\n    63\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    64\t    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(evidence_ids))})',\n    65\t                        evidence_ids).fetchall()\n    66\t    return {e: {'text': (q or '')[:400], 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef pair_family(draw, total, dc):\n    70\t    return {'members': {total[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, total[0])},\n    71\t                        dc[0]: {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'bands': bands(draw, dc[0])}},\n    72\t            'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': dc[0], 'whole': total[0]}],\n    73\t            'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    74\t            'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027']}\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef only(family, view_id):\n    78\t    out = {'members': {view_id: family['members'][view_id]}, 'relations': [], 'shared': family['shared'], 'compare_periods': []}\n    79\t    if 'part_scopes' in family:                                         # [53] the separate arm keeps S8's part-of scopes (D738)\n    80\t        out['part_scopes'] = family['part_scopes']\n    81\t    return out\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef small_family(family, part_scopes=(), notes=None):\n    85\t    \"\"\"[D737] A family for the small format: each member's unit (USD bn: the bands are in billions), the part-of scopes S8 reads, and\n    86\t    any note on a member's key.\"\"\"\n    87\t    out = json.loads(json.dumps(family))\n    88\t    for v, m in out['members'].items():\n    89\t        m['unit'] = 'USD bn'\n    90\t        if notes and v in notes:\n    91\t            m['key_note'] = notes[v]\n    92\t    out['part_scopes'] = list(part_scopes)\n    93\t    return out\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\tPAIR_SCOPES = [{'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'part': 'Data Center', 'whole': 'company'}]\n    97\tO_NOTE = 'the balance at the end of FY2027, as the FY2027 annual report publishes it'\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tdef checker(fmt):\n   101\t    return CHECKERS[fmt]\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\tdef decode(data, fmt, family):\n   105\t    \"\"\"The stored wire answer in the shape the checks and packets read, by the plan's format.\"\"\"\n   106\t    return cs.from_answer(data, family) if fmt == 'v13s' else strip(data)\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef questions(draw, view_ids):\n   110\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUN / draw / \"prod/views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   111\t    out = {}\n   112\t    for v in view_ids:\n   113\t        q = conn.execute('select question from views where view_id=?', (v,)).fetchone()[0]\n   114\t        ladder = [c for (c,) in conn.execute('select condition from rungs where view_id=? order by position', (v,))]\n   115\t        out[v] = {'question': q, 'ladder': ladder}\n   116\t    return out\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\tdef shown_lines(user):\n   120\t    \"\"\"Each evidence item exactly as the request showed it: its header line (tier, speaker, original source and date) and its quote.\"\"\"\n   121\t    m = re.search(r'\\[Evidence in view for the family, \\d+ items\\]\\n(.*?)(?:\\n\\n\\[|\\n\\nAnswer per)', user, re.S)\n   122\t    out = {}\n   123\t    for chunk in re.split(r'\\n(?=- e\\d+ )', m.group(1) if m else ''):\n   124\t        if chunk.startswith('- e'):\n   125\t            out[chunk[2:].split(' ', 1)[0]] = chunk\n   350\t        rename = {f['id']: f'{view_id}.{f[\"id\"]}' for f in calc['figures']}\n   351\t        figs = {f['id']: f for f in calc['figures']}\n   352\t        refs = lambda f, figs=figs: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   353\t            ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   354\t        try:\n   355\t            values = ck._evaluate_bounded(figs, refs, {})\n   356\t        except Exception:\n   357\t            values = {}\n   358\t        for f in calc['figures']:\n   359\t            g = dict(f, id=rename[f['id']])\n   360\t            for key in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   361\t                if key in g:\n   362\t                    g[key] = [rename.get(x, x) for x in g[key]]\n   363\t            for key in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   364\t                if key in g:\n   365\t                    g[key] = rename.get(g[key], g[key])\n   366\t            if 'adjusts' in g:\n   367\t                g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=rename.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   368\t            figures.append(g)\n   369\t            recomputed[g['id']] = values.get(f['id'])\n   370\t            owner[g['id']] = view_id\n   371\t            units[g['id']] = f.get('unit')\n   372\t        for a in calc['answers']:\n   373\t            a2 = dict(a)\n   374\t            if 'outcome' in a2:\n   375\t                a2['outcome'] = rename.get(a2['outcome'], a2['outcome'])\n   376\t            if a2.get('reference', {}).get('figure'):\n   377\t                a2['reference'] = {'figure': rename.get(a2['reference']['figure'], a2['reference']['figure'])}\n   378\t            answers.append(a2)\n   379\t    key = lambda f: (f['what']['population'], f['what']['measure'], f['what']['scope'], f['what']['period'], f.get('scenario', 'base'))\n   380\t    candidates = {}\n   381\t    for g in figures:\n   382\t        if g.get('basis') == 'forecast' and ck._key(g['what']) in shared_keys:\n   383\t            candidates.setdefault(key(g), {}).setdefault(owner[g['id']], []).append(g['id'])\n   384\t    alias, duplicates = {}, []\n   385\t    for k, by_call in candidates.items():                  # [47d.2] one to one: each call holds exactly one candidate\n   386\t        if len(by_call) == 2 and all(len(ids) == 1 for ids in by_call.values()):\n   387\t            (a,), (b,) = (by_call[v] for v, _ in parts)\n   388\t            if units[a] == units[b] and _same_value(recomputed.get(a), recomputed.get(b)):   # [47b.1] equal values, [47e.2] in one unit\n   389\t                alias[b] = a\n   390\t    if alias:\n   391\t        kept = []\n   392\t        for g in figures:\n   393\t            if g['id'] in alias:\n   394\t                duplicates.append(g)\n   395\t                continue\n   396\t            for k2 in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   397\t                if k2 in g:\n   398\t                    g[k2] = [alias.get(x, x) for x in g[k2]]\n   399\t            for k2 in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   400\t                if k2 in g:\n   401\t                    g[k2] = alias.get(g[k2], g[k2])\n   402\t            if 'adjusts' in g:\n   403\t                g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=alias.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   404\t            kept.append(g)\n   405\t        figures = kept\n   406\t        for a in answers:\n   407\t            if a.get('outcome') in alias:\n   408\t                a['outcome'] = alias[a['outcome']]\n   409\t            if a.get('reference', {}).get('figure') in alias:\n   410\t                a['reference'] = {'figure': alias[a['reference']['figure']]}\n   411\t    return {'figures': figures, 'answers': answers, 'unified': [{'kept': alias[d['id']], 'duplicate': d} for d in duplicates]}\n   412\t\n   413\t\n   414\tdef recover(out):\n   415\t    \"\"\"Read-only: rebuild results.json from the journal of a stopped run; nothing is sent.\"\"\"\n   416\t    items = json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())\n   417\t    ledger = json.loads((out / 'ledger.json').read_text()) if (out / 'ledger.json').exists() else None\n   418\t    summary = summarise(out, items, ledger)\n   419\t    print(json.dumps({'damaged': summary['damaged'], 'finals': {k: v['decision'] for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}}, indent=1))\n   420\t    return summary\n   421\t\n   422\t\n   423\tdef budget_module():\n   424\t    import importlib.util\n   425\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('budget_replay_v13', REPO / 'clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py')\n   426\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   427\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n   428\t    return module\n   429\t\n   430\t\n   431\tdef send(out, approved, plan_path):\n   432\t    if APPROVED_CEILING is None or approved != APPROVED_CEILING:\n   433\t        raise SystemExit(f'the approved ceiling is {APPROVED_CEILING} (Alex names it); refused')\n   434\t    if out.exists():\n   435\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} exists: the gate starts from an empty folder')\n   436\t    text = Path(plan_path).read_text()\n   437\t    items = json.loads(text)\n   438\t    formats = {i.get('format') for i in items}\n   439\t    if formats == {'v13s'}:                                                  # D753: the v13s re-send has its own pin and authorization\n   440\t        pin, auth = PINNED_PLAN_V13S, AUTH_V13S\n   441\t    elif 'v13s' in formats:\n   442\t        raise SystemExit('the plan mixes formats; refused')\n   443\t    else:\n   444\t        pin, auth = PINNED_PLAN_SHA256, AUTH\n   445\t    if pin is None or hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest() != pin:          # [47.2] only the reviewed plan\n   446\t        raise SystemExit('the plan is not the reviewed one (sha256 differs); refused')\n   447\t    auth.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   448\t    try:                                                                     # [47.2] one authorization, one ledger, one launch\n   449\t        with open(auth, 'x') as handle:\n   450\t            json.dump({'plan_sha256': pin, 'ceiling': approved, 'out': str(out)}, handle)\n   451\t    except FileExistsError:\n   452\t        raise SystemExit(f'{auth} exists: this authorization was already used; refused')\n   453\t    if len({(i['unit'], i['arm']) for i in items}) != len(items):\n   454\t        raise SystemExit('duplicate (unit, arm) in the plan; refused')\n   455\t    out.mkdir(parents=True)\n   456\t    (out / 'plan.json').write_text(json.dumps(items))\n   457\t    budget = budget_module()\n   458\t    budget.SharedLedger.init(str(out / 'ledger.json'), approved)\n   459\t    ledger = budget.SharedLedger(str(out / 'ledger.json'))\n   460\t    lock_handle = open(out / 'gate.launcher.lock', 'a+')\n   461\t    if not ledger.claim_launcher('v13-gate', lock_handle):\n   462\t        raise SystemExit('another launch is running')\n   463\t    remove_gate = budget.install_stop_gate(ledger)\n   464\t    try:\n   465\t        summary = Gate(out, budget.BudgetTransport(ledger), ledger).run(items)\n   466\t    finally:\n   467\t        remove_gate()\n   468\t        ledger.remove_launcher('v13-gate')\n   469\t    print(json.dumps({k: v.get('decision') for k, v in summary['finals'].items()}, indent=1))\n   470\t\n   471\t\n   472\t# ---------- blind reading ----------\n   473\tQUESTIONS = {'usable': 'the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on',\n   474\t             'contradiction': 'with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction',\n   475\t             'internal_reference': \"the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation\",\n   476\t             'deciding_gap': 'an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band'}\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\tFIGURE_TOKEN = re.compile(r'\\b([A-Za-z0-9]*F\\d+)\\b')\n   480\tPASSAGE_TOKEN = re.compile(r'\\b(e\\d+)\\b')\n   481\tPASSAGE_RANGE = re.compile(r'\\be(\\d+)\\s*[-–]\\s*e?(\\d+)\\b')\n   482\t\n   483\t\n   484\tdef renamed_text(text, rename):\n   485\t    \"\"\"[D753, council 70] Figure ids inside prose follow the renumbering, so a reference in the reasons still points to the figure the\n   486\t    writer meant; an id the card does not show is left as written.\"\"\"\n   487\t    return FIGURE_TOKEN.sub(lambda m: rename.get(m.group(1), m.group(1)), text) if isinstance(text, str) else text\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\tdef named_in_text(text, figure_ids, shown_passages):\n   491\t    \"\"\"[D753, council 70] The figure ids and passage ids a prose field names, a written range e5399-e5404 included in full.\"\"\"\n   492\t    if not isinstance(text, str):\n   493\t        return set(), set()\n   494\t    figures = {t for t in FIGURE_TOKEN.findall(text) if t in figure_ids}\n   495\t    passages = {t for t in PASSAGE_TOKEN.findall(text) if t in shown_passages}\n   496\t    for lo, hi in PASSAGE_RANGE.findall(text):        # every shown passage inside a written range (council 70b: no width limit)\n   497\t        lo, hi = int(lo), int(hi)\n   498\t        if hi > lo:\n   499\t            passages |= {f'e{n}' for n in range(lo, hi + 1) if f'e{n}' in shown_passages}\n   500\t    return figures, passages\n   501\t\n   502\t\n   503\tdef normalise(calc, prefix=''):\n   504\t    \"\"\"Figure ids renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) and member prefixes removed, so the arm cannot be read from the ids. Ids named in\n   505\t    prose (reasons, why, basis_text) are renumbered with them.\"\"\"\n   506\t    rename = {f['id']: f'{prefix}F{n}' for n, f in enumerate(calc['figures'], 1)}\n   507\t    out = []\n   508\t    for f in calc['figures']:\n   509\t        g = dict(f, id=rename[f['id']])\n   510\t        if 'basis_text' in g:\n   511\t            g['basis_text'] = renamed_text(g['basis_text'], rename)\n   512\t        for key in ('inputs', 'rests_on', 'converts'):\n   513\t            if key in g:\n   514\t                g[key] = [rename.get(x, x) for x in g[key]]\n   515\t        for key in ('disputed', 'bridge'):\n   516\t            if key in g:\n   517\t                g[key] = rename.get(g[key], g[key])\n   518\t        if 'adjusts' in g:\n   519\t            g['adjusts'] = dict(g['adjusts'], figure=rename.get(g['adjusts']['figure'], g['adjusts']['figure']))\n   520\t        out.append(g)\n   521\t    answers = []\n   522\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   523\t        a2 = dict(a)\n   524\t        for key in ('reasons', 'why'):\n   525\t            if key in a2:\n   526\t                a2[key] = renamed_text(a2[key], rename)\n   527\t        if isinstance((a2.get('reference') or {}).get('unavailable'), str):\n   528\t            a2['reference'] = {'unavailable': renamed_text(a2['reference']['unavailable'], rename)}\n   529\t        if 'outcome' in a2:\n   530\t            a2['outcome'] = rename.get(a2['outcome'], a2['outcome'])\n   531\t        if (a2.get('reference') or {}).get('figure'):\n   532\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': rename.get(a2['reference']['figure'], a2['reference']['figure'])}\n   533\t        answers.append(a2)\n   534\t    return {'figures': out, 'answers': answers}, rename\n   535\t\n   536\t\n   537\tdef run_digest(out):\n   538\t    h = hashlib.sha256()\n   539\t    for name in ('answers.jsonl', 'retries.jsonl', 'results.json', 'plan.json'):\n   540\t        path = out / name\n   541\t        h.update(name.encode() + b'\\0' + (path.read_bytes() if path.exists() else b''))\n   542\t    return h.hexdigest()\n   543\t\n   544\t\n   545\tdef card_view(calc, view_id, recorded, prefix='', ck=cc, shown=()):\n   546\t    \"\"\"[47b.3] One card as its own derivation: the figures its outcome and reference rest on, renumbered F1.. (after `prefix`) for this\n   547\t    card alone, and the recorded assumptions about its outcome or its own figures mapped to the same numbers. [D753, council 70] It also\n   548\t    shows every figure and passage the card's prose names (reasons, why, the reference's unavailability, and the basis of a shown\n   549\t    figure), with what those figures rest on, so an unresolved card keeps the passages it weighed and no prose reference dangles.\"\"\"\n   550\t    figs = {f['id']: f for f in calc['figures']}\n   551\t    refs = lambda f: list(f.get('inputs', [])) + [r for r in f.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs] + \\\n   552\t        ([f['adjusts']['figure']] if f.get('adjusts') else []) + ([f['bridge']] if f.get('bridge') else [])\n   553\t    ans = next(a for a in calc['answers'] if a['view_id'] == view_id)\n   554\t    shown = set(shown)\n   555\t    own, text_passages = set(), set()\n   556\t    starts = {ans.get('outcome'), (ans.get('reference') or {}).get('figure')} - {None}\n   557\t    for key in ('reasons', 'why'):\n   558\t        found, passages = named_in_text(ans.get(key), figs, shown)\n   559\t        starts |= found\n   560\t        text_passages |= passages\n   561\t    found, passages = named_in_text((ans.get('reference') or {}).get('unavailable'), figs, shown)\n   562\t    starts |= found\n   563\t    text_passages |= passages\n   564\t    while starts:                                         # the closure over figures named in the prose of figures already shown\n   565\t        for start in [s for s in starts if s in figs]:\n   566\t            own |= ck._upstream_of(start, figs, refs) | {start}\n   567\t        starts = set()\n   568\t        for fid in own:\n   569\t            found, passages = named_in_text(figs[fid].get('basis_text'), figs, shown)\n   570\t            starts |= found - own\n   571\t            text_passages |= passages\n   572\t    sub = {'figures': [f for f in calc['figures'] if f['id'] in own], 'answers': [ans]}\n   573\t    norm, rename = normalise(sub, prefix)\n   574\t    mapped = []\n   575\t    for r in recorded:                                    # an assumption about this card's outcome, or about one of its own figures\n   576\t        named = [r[k] for k in ('figure', 'bridge') if isinstance(r.get(k), str)]\n   577\t        if (r.get('outcome') == view_id or any(n in rename for n in named)) and all(n in rename for n in named):\n   578\t            mapped.append({k: rename[v] if k in ('figure', 'bridge') else v for k, v in r.items()})\n   579\t    pushed = {p.get('evidence_id') or p.get('evidence') for p in ans.get('pushes') or [] if isinstance(p, dict)} - {None}\n   580\t    return norm, mapped, sorted({f['evidence'] for f in sub['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} | set(ans.get('cites', []))\n   581\t                                | {x for f in sub['figures'] for x in f.get('rests_on', []) if str(x).startswith('e')} | text_passages\n   582\t                                | pushed)                     # council 70b: the passages the card weighs in its pushes\n   583\t\n   584\t\n   585\tNO_ANSWER = {'not sent': 'No request was sent for this card.', 'interrupted': 'The request was started; no answer was recorded.',\n   586\t             'transport': 'No answer arrived.', 'retry not sent': 'The answer was refused and its retry was not sent.'}\n   587\tFORMAT_INVALID = 'The answer did not match the required format.'\n   588\t\n   589\t\n   590\tdef packet_units(results, items):\n   591\t    \"\"\"Every packet the run gives, as (unit, arm, draw) -> (decision, per-card source): the joint and singleton answers from the finals,\n   592\t    the separate arm's reconciled pairs with each card's own separate answer.\"\"\"\n   593\t    units = {}\n   594\t    for key, entry in results['finals'].items():\n   595\t        unit, arm, draw = key.split('|')\n   596\t        if not arm.startswith('separate-'):\n   597\t            first = first_attempt(entry)                    # [47e.1] the first attempt is scored on both arms\n   598\t            units[(unit, arm, draw)] = (first.get('decision'), {v: first for v in items[(unit, arm)]['members']})\n   599\t    for key, entry in results['reconciled'].items():\n   600\t        unit, draw = key.split('|')\n   601\t        per_card = {a.split('-', 1)[1]: first_attempt(results['finals'].get(f'{unit}|{a}|{draw}', {})) for (u, a) in items\n   602\t                    if u == unit and a.startswith('separate-')}\n   603\t        units[(unit, 'separate', draw)] = (entry.get('decision'), per_card)\n   604\t    return units\n   605\t\n   606\t\n   607\tdef card_lines(base, fam, v, token, data, final_label, prefix=''):\n   608\t    \"\"\"One card's answer as a reader sees it: the passages it names, its own figures, its recomputed outcome and assumptions, the card.\n   609\t    Returns (lines, ids a ground may name).\"\"\"\n   610\t    if not data:\n   611\t        return [f'  {final_label}'], set()\n   612\t    fmt = base.get('format')\n   613\t    calc = decode(data, fmt, fam)\n   614\t    try:\n   615\t        checked = checker(fmt).check(fam, base['passages'], calc)\n   616\t    except Exception as error:\n   617\t        checked = {'errors': [('checker', str(error))], 'recorded': [], 'published': {}}\n   618\t    try:\n   619\t        norm, recorded, named = card_view(calc, v, checked.get('recorded', []), prefix, checker(fmt), base.get('shown', {}))\n   620\t    except StopIteration:\n   621\t        return ['  The answer has no card for this question.'], set()\n   622\t    lines = ['  Passages, as the request showed them:\\n' + '\\n'.join('  ' + base['shown'].get(e, f'- {e} (not shown)') for e in named),\n   623\t             '  Figures (declared):\\n' + '\\n'.join(f'  - {json.dumps(f, ensure_ascii=False)}' for f in norm['figures']),\n   624\t             '  Recomputed outcome: ' + json.dumps((checked.get('published') or {}).get(v)),\n   625\t             '  Recorded assumptions: ' + json.dumps(recorded),\n   626\t             f'  Card {token}: ' + json.dumps(norm['answers'][0], ensure_ascii=False)]\n   627\t    return lines, set(named) | {f['id'] for f in norm['figures']}\n   628\t\n   629\t\n   630\tdef packet_body(items, unit, arm, decision, per_card):\n   631\t    \"\"\"[47d.3, 47e.1] One scoring packet: each card's scored (first) answer only. No attempt history, no code decision and no check code,\n   632\t    which would tell separate calls from one joint call; the verdict applies the code's decision itself. Returns (lines, grounds, members).\"\"\"\n   633\t    base = items[(unit, 'joint' if unit.startswith('pair') else 'single')]\n   634\t    grounds, lines = set(), []\n   635\t    for number, v in enumerate(base['members'], 1):\n   636\t        q = base['questions'][v]\n   637\t        token = f'K{number}'\n   638\t        grounds.add(token)\n   639\t        lines.append(f'### Card {token}: {q[\"question\"]}\\n  Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {i + 1}: {c}' for i, c in enumerate(q['ladder'])))\n   640\t        source = per_card.get(v, {})                         # the scored (first) attempt of this card\n   641\t        label = NO_ANSWER.get(source.get('decision'), FORMAT_INVALID if source.get('status') == 'format invalid' else NO_ANSWER['not sent'])\n   642\t        fam = base['family'] if arm != 'separate' else only(base['family'], v)\n   643\t        body, named = card_lines(base, fam, v, token, source.get('data'), label)\n   644\t        lines += body\n   645\t        grounds |= named\n   646\t    lines.append('For each card answer yes or no, each with a ground that names a card (K...), passage (e...) or figure (F...) of this packet: '\n   647\t                 + '; '.join(f'{k}: {t}' for k, t in QUESTIONS.items()) + '\\n')\n   648\t    return lines, sorted(grounds), base['members']\n   649\t\n   650\t\n   651\tdef key_commitment(key):\n   652\t    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(key, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n   653\t\n   654\t\n   655\tdef render_packets(out, key):\n   656\t    \"\"\"The scoring packets for a key {salt, run_digest, order}: the key's salted sha256 first (so the text the readers receive commits\n   657\t    to the mapping), then each packet in the key's order, rendered from the run's results and plan.\"\"\"\n   658\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   659\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   660\t    units = packet_units(results, items)\n   661\t    lines, rendered = [f'Key commitment: {key_commitment(key)}', ''], {}\n   662\t    for pid, unit_key in key['order']:\n   663\t        decision, per_card = units[tuple(unit_key)]\n   664\t        body, grounds, members = packet_body(items, unit_key[0], unit_key[1], decision, per_card)\n   665\t        lines += [f'## {pid}'] + body\n   666\t        rendered[pid] = {'unit': unit_key[0], 'arm': unit_key[1], 'draw': unit_key[2], 'decision': decision, 'grounds': grounds,\n   667\t                         'cards': {f'K{n}': v for n, v in enumerate(members, 1)}}\n   668\t    return '\\n'.join(lines), rendered, units\n   669\t\n   670\t\n   671\tdef returned_text(raw):\n   672\t    \"\"\"The model's text inside a stored provider response, or the stored response itself when it cannot be read.\"\"\"\n   673\t    if not raw:\n   674\t        return '(no text was stored)'\n   675\t    try:\n   676\t        message = json.loads(raw)['choices'][0]['message']\n   677\t    except (ValueError, KeyError, IndexError, TypeError):\n   678\t        return str(raw)\n   679\t    if not isinstance(message, dict):\n   680\t        return str(raw)\n   681\t    if isinstance(message.get('content'), str):\n   682\t        return message['content']\n   683\t    if message.get('refusal'):\n   684\t        return f'(the model refused: {message[\"refusal\"]})'\n   685\t    return f'(no text returned: {json.dumps(message, ensure_ascii=False)})'\n   686\t\n   687\t\n   688\tdef render_attempts(out, labels):\n   689\t    \"\"\"[47d.3, 47e.3] For diagnostic reading only, never scored: every retry and every returned text that failed the format check, each\n   690\t    under its own shuffled label (D01..), with the question, that attempt's own answer (or the text returned and the passages it names),\n   691\t    and no link to a packet.\"\"\"\n   692\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   693\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   694\t    lines = []\n   695\t    for label, (unit, arm, draw, v, attempt) in labels:\n   696\t        entry = results['finals'][f'{unit}|{arm}|{draw}']\n   697\t        a = next(x for x in entry['attempts'] if x['attempt'] == attempt)\n   698\t        base = items[(unit, 'joint' if unit.startswith('pair') else 'single')]\n   699\t        fam = base['family'] if arm in ('joint', 'single') else only(base['family'], v)\n   700\t        lines.append(f'## {label}: {base[\"questions\"][v][\"question\"]}')\n   701\t        if a.get('status') == 'format invalid':\n   702\t            returned = returned_text(a.get('raw'))\n   703\t            named = sorted(set(re.findall(r'\\be\\d+\\b', returned)) & set(base['shown']))\n   704\t            lines.append(f'  {FORMAT_INVALID} The text returned:\\n' + '\\n'.join('    ' + l for l in returned.splitlines()))\n   705\t            if named:\n   706\t                lines.append('  Passages it names, as the request showed them:\\n' + '\\n'.join('  ' + base['shown'][e] for e in named))\n   707\t            continue\n   708\t        lines += card_lines(base, fam, v, 'K1', a.get('data'), NO_ANSWER.get(a.get('decision'), NO_ANSWER['transport']), 'T.')[0]\n   709\t    return '\\n'.join(lines)\n   710\t\n   711\t\n   712\tdef packets(out, key_dir):\n   713\t    if (key_dir / 'packet-key.json').exists():            # [47b.4] the inventory and key are frozen once made\n   714\t        raise SystemExit(f'{key_dir / \"packet-key.json\"} exists: the packets are frozen; refused')\n   715\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   716\t    items = {(i['unit'], i['arm']): i for i in json.loads((out / 'plan.json').read_text())}\n   717\t    rng = random.Random(secrets.randbits(64))\n   718\t    unit_keys = sorted(packet_units(results, items))\n   719\t    rng.shuffle(unit_keys)\n   720\t    earlier = sorted((k.split('|')[0], k.split('|')[1], k.split('|')[2], v, a['attempt'])     # every retry, and every format failure\n   721\t                     for k, e in results['finals'].items() for a in (e.get('attempts') or [])\n   722\t                     if a['attempt'] >= 2 or a.get('status') == 'format invalid'\n   723\t                     for v in items[tuple(k.split('|')[:2])]['members'])\n   724\t    rng.shuffle(earlier)\n   725\t    key = {'salt': secrets.token_hex(16), 'run_digest': run_digest(out), 'order': [(f'P{n:02d}', list(u)) for n, u in enumerate(unit_keys, 1)],\n   726\t           'attempts': [(f'D{n:02d}', list(e)) for n, e in enumerate(earlier, 1)]}\n   727\t    text = render_packets(out, key)[0]\n   728\t    attempts_text = render_attempts(out, key['attempts'])          # [47f.2] both rendered before anything is written\n   729\t    if (out / 'packets.md').exists() or (out / 'attempts.md').exists():\n   730\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} already holds packets; refused')\n   731\t    key_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   732\t    with open(key_dir / 'packet-key.json', 'x') as handle:\n   733\t        json.dump(key, handle, indent=1)\n   734\t    with open(out / 'packets.md', 'x') as handle:\n   735\t        handle.write(text)\n   736\t    with open(out / 'attempts.md', 'x') as handle:\n   737\t        handle.write(attempts_text)\n   738\t    print(f'{len(key[\"order\"])} packets, {len(key[\"attempts\"])} diagnostic attempts; key in {key_dir}')\n   739\t\n   740\t\n   741\tdef _grounded(ground, grounds):\n   742\t    \"\"\"[47b.4] A ground is non-empty text that names at least one card, passage or figure of the packet.\"\"\"\n   743\t    return isinstance(ground, str) and ground.strip() != '' and any(re.search(rf'\\b{re.escape(g)}\\b', ground) for g in grounds)\n   744\t\n   745\t\n   746\tdef final_readings(pid, cards, members, grounds=()):\n   747\t    \"\"\"[47.4] Two independent readings per card (A, B), each question answered yes/no with its ground; a third decides each\n   748\t    disagreement. Returns ({card: {question: answer}}, problems).\"\"\"\n   749\t    problems, final = [], {}\n   750\t    if sorted(cards) != sorted(members):\n   751\t        return None, [f'{pid}: cards {sorted(cards)} are not the unit\\'s {sorted(members)}']\n   752\t    for v, r in cards.items():\n   753\t        final[v] = {}\n   754\t        for q in QUESTIONS:\n   755\t            a, b = (r.get(x, {}).get(q, {}) for x in ('A', 'B'))\n   756\t            for name, x in (('A', a), ('B', b)):\n   757\t                if x.get('answer') not in ('yes', 'no') or not _grounded(x.get('ground'), grounds):\n   758\t                    problems.append(f'{pid} {v} {q}: reader {name} gave no yes/no with a ground from this packet')\n   759\t            if a.get('answer') == b.get('answer'):\n   760\t                final[v][q] = a.get('answer')\n   761\t            else:\n   762\t                t = r.get('third', {}).get(q, {})\n   763\t                if t.get('answer') not in ('yes', 'no') or not _grounded(t.get('ground'), grounds):\n   764\t                    problems.append(f'{pid} {v} {q}: the readers disagree and no third reading decides')\n   765\t                final[v][q] = t.get('answer')\n   766\t    return final, problems\n   767\t\n   768\t\n   769\tdef verdict(out, readings_path, key_dir):\n   770\t    \"\"\"[47e.4] Seal the readings into the run (readings.json, created once), compute D725's lines once and write verdict.json bound to\n   771\t    the readings, the key and the packets. A second verdict on the run is refused; `replay` recomputes and compares.\"\"\"\n   772\t    if (out / 'verdict.json').exists() or (out / 'readings.json').exists():\n   773\t        raise SystemExit(f'{out} already has sealed readings or a verdict; refused (use replay)')\n   774\t    data = Path(readings_path).read_bytes()\n   775\t    with open(out / 'readings.json', 'xb') as handle:\n   776\t        handle.write(data)\n   777\t    summary = score(out, key_dir)\n   778\t    frozen = json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   779\t    record = {'readings_sha256': hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(), 'key_commitment': key_commitment(frozen),\n   780\t              'packets_sha256': hashlib.sha256((out / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest() if (out / 'packets.md').exists() else None,\n   781\t              'run_digest': run_digest(out), 'summary': summary}\n   782\t    with open(out / 'verdict.json', 'x') as handle:\n   783\t        json.dump(record, handle, indent=1)\n   784\t    return summary\n   785\t\n   786\t\n   787\tdef replay(out, key_dir):\n   788\t    \"\"\"Recompute the verdict from the sealed readings and compare it with verdict.json.\"\"\"\n   789\t    record = json.loads((out / 'verdict.json').read_text())\n   790\t    data = (out / 'readings.json').read_bytes()\n   791\t    same = (hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest() == record['readings_sha256'] and record['run_digest'] == run_digest(out)\n   792\t            and record['key_commitment'] == key_commitment(json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())))\n   793\t    summary = score(out, key_dir)\n   794\t    matches = same and summary == record['summary']\n   795\t    print(json.dumps({'reproduced': matches}, indent=1))\n   796\t    return matches\n   797\t\n   798\t\n   799\tdef score(out, key_dir):\n   800\t    \"\"\"D725's registered lines on the sealed readings, bound to this run.\"\"\"\n   801\t    frozen = json.loads((key_dir / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   802\t    submitted = json.loads((out / 'readings.json').read_text())\n   803\t    problems = [] if frozen.get('run_digest') == run_digest(out) else ['the packet key does not belong to this run']   # [47b.4]\n   804\t    text, key, units = render_packets(out, frozen)                  # [47c.2] every packet rendered again from the run\n   805\t    if sorted(tuple(u) for _, u in frozen['order']) != sorted(units):\n   806\t        problems.append('the key does not map one packet to each unit of the run')\n   807\t    sha = hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()\n   808\t    packets_path = out / 'packets.md'\n   809\t    written = packets_path.read_text() if packets_path.exists() else ''\n   810\t    if not written.startswith(f'Key commitment: {key_commitment(frozen)}\\n'):      # [47d.1] the mapping the readers' text committed to\n   811\t        problems.append('the key is not the one packets.md committed to')\n   812\t    if hashlib.sha256(written.encode()).hexdigest() != sha:\n   813\t        problems.append('packets.md is not the text the run and the key give')\n   814\t    if submitted.get('packets_sha256') != sha:\n   815\t        problems.append('the readings were not made on the frozen packets')\n   816\t    readings = submitted.get('packets', {})\n   817\t    results = json.loads((out / 'results.json').read_text())\n   818\t    problems += [f'answers.jsonl line {d[\"line\"]} is damaged' for d in results.get('damaged', [])\n   819\t                 if d.get('journal') == 'answers.jsonl']                     # [47g] a damaged retry record stays diagnostic\n   820\t    scored = {k: first_attempt(v)['decision'] for k, v in results['finals'].items()}            # [47f.1] completeness from the scored attempts\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
