{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md | tail -140; ls docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'","aggregated_output":"   181\t  - the scoring text has no attempt, decision or code;\n   182\t  - the refused first answer appears only in `attempts.md`;\n   183\t  - a swap of identical-text packets is INCOMPLETE;\n   184\t  - a forged key is INCOMPLETE;\n   185\t  - two equal shared forecasts in the second call are refused (C4, three nodes);\n   186\t  - an interrupted card says the request was started.\n   187\t- **Mutants:** 20 of 20 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   188\t\n   189\t## 3f. After council round 47e (`codex-r47e.md`)\n   190\t\n   191\t- **[47e.1] The first attempt is scored, on both arms.**\n   192\t  - In the joint arm, a cross-card conflict (C3) is refused and retried with its reason, so the retry can repair it. In the separate\n   193\t    arm, the same conflict appears only when the two answers are reconciled, after both calls are over, and there is no retry.\n   194\t  - Scoring the final answers would credit the joint arm with a second chance the separate arm cannot have.\n   195\t  - D725 registered both arms \"under the same format and checks\" and says nothing about retries. Its pass and stop lines stay as\n   196\t    written and are applied to the first attempts.\n   197\t  - Retries are still sent and read for diagnosis (`attempts.md`), and are not counted.\n   198\t  - Rehearsed: the joint pair is published after its retry, but its refused first attempt is scored, so both arms come out at 6.\n   199\t- **[47e.2] One unit.** A shared forecast is unified only when the two copies have the same unit, as well as the same value and bounds.\n   200\t  Rehearsed: 110 USD bn against 110 USD is refused (C4).\n   201\t- **[47e.3] Every returned text is readable.**\n   202\t  - When the format check fails an answer, the scoring packet keeps its neutral label.\n   203\t  - The text the model returned, and the passages it names, go to `attempts.md` under a blind label. This covers both a first attempt\n   204\t    and a final one that fails the format.\n   205\t- **[47e.4] One verdict per run.**\n   206\t  - `verdict` copies the readings into the run once (`readings.json`, created exclusively).\n   207\t  - It scores them and writes `verdict.json` once, holding the readings' sha256, the key commitment, the packets' sha256, the run digest\n   208\t    and the result.\n   209\t  - A second verdict on the run is refused. `paid_gate.py replay` recomputes from the sealed readings and must reproduce the result.\n   210\t  - Rehearsed: the second verdict is refused; replay reproduces the result; after the sealed readings are edited, replay fails.\n   211\t- **Rehearsal:** 55 of 55, run three times (`rehearsal.log`).\n   212\t- **Mutants:** 25 of 25 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   213\t  - Two obsolete mutants were repointed or removed.\n   214\t  - One mutant crashed on a missing file and not on the defence. The test was corrected, and the mutant now fails the right check.\n   215\t\n   216\t## 3g. After council round 47f (`codex-r47f.md`)\n   217\t\n   218\t- **[47f.1] Retries cannot decide whether the scored test is complete.**\n   219\t  - The run sends every first attempt (all 36) before any retry.\n   220\t  - Completeness is judged on the first attempts: each must end published, held or refused.\n   221\t  - A retry that fails in transport, is interrupted or is never sent stays in the diagnostic record.\n   222\t  - Rehearsed: an interruption during a retry leaves all 36 scored attempts and a complete verdict. A transport failure on a retry\n   223\t    leaves the verdict complete. An interruption during a scored attempt makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. In the journal, every first\n   224\t    attempt comes before every retry.\n   225\t- **[47f.2] Every returned text survives.**\n   226\t  - The record keeps the provider's whole response, as the archive stores it, with no 20,000-character cut.\n   227\t  - A null content is shown as the model's refusal, or as \"no text returned\".\n   228\t  - Both files are rendered before anything is written, and a failed render leaves no files.\n   229\t  - Rehearsed: a refusal with null content, a 25,000-character malformed answer whose passage is named at its end, and a render that\n   230\t    fails and then succeeds.\n   231\t- **Rehearsal:** 61 of 61, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   232\t- **Mutants:** 30 of 30 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`). Two mutants are caught by the crash the defence prevents:\n   233\t  - without the interrupted branch, the summary fails on an unfinished attempt;\n   234\t  - passing a null content on, packet rendering fails.\n   235\t\n   236\t## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n   237\t\n   238\t- **[47g] Two journals, read on the writer's own delimiter.**\n   239\t  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n   240\t  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n   241\t    interrupted, but leaves the scored test complete.\n   242\t  - Records are split on '\\n' only, the writer's delimiter. An answer may contain other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+0085,\n   243\t    U+2029), and these are kept inside the record.\n   244\t  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n   245\t    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n   246\t    provider's own call sequence.\n   247\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   248\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   249\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   250\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   251\t\n   252\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   253\t\n   254\t- **Packets:** 27 (`paid_gate.py packets`): 9 joint pair-draws, 9 reconciled separate pair-draws and 9 singleton draws. The labels are\n   255\t  shuffled, the arm is hidden, and the key is kept in `~/.hivemind-keys/v13-paid-gate/`.\n   256\t  - Each packet shows, per card (K1, K2), the question, the ladder, every passage the final answer names (as the request showed it),\n   257\t    its figures, the recomputed outcome, the recorded assumptions and the card. Nothing about attempts or the code's decision is\n   258\t    shown (§3e).\n   259\t  - A packet the code did not publish (held, unresolved, not reconciled) is read too. The verdict, not the reader, applies the code's\n   260\t    decision: its cards cannot count as usable.\n   261\t  - The readers receive `packets.md` exactly, with its key-commitment line. The readings file carries that text's sha256.\n   262\t- **Readers:** two fresh readers of different families, a Codex session and a Claude subagent, each blind to the other and to the arm.\n   263\t  For each card each answers four questions, yes or no, with the passage that decides:\n   264\t  1. **usable:** the outcome is usable and supported by the shown passages it rests on;\n   265\t  2. **contradiction:** with the other card of its packet, it states a hard numerical contradiction;\n   266\t  3. **internal_reference:** the system's own forecast is presented as the market's expectation;\n   267\t  4. **deciding_gap:** an unresolved overlap, a change of scope or an unsized adjustment decides its band.\n   268\t- **Agreement:** where the two readers agree, that is the reading. Where they disagree, a third fresh reader (Codex) reads the card with\n   269\t  both readings and the passages, and its answer decides. No reading is changed after the verdict is computed.\n   270\t- **Verdict** (`paid_gate.py verdict`, D725's lines, on the first attempts; computed once and sealed, §3f):\n   271\t  - **PASS:** the joint arm has both cards usable in at least 8 of 9 pairs, at least 2 of 3 per snapshot, and at least 3 more usable\n   272\t    pairs than the separate arm; and zero published defects (contradiction, internal reference or deciding gap) across the joint and\n   273\t    singleton answers.\n   274\t  - **STOP:** any such published defect; a coverage line missed; a gain under 3.\n   275\t  - **INCOMPLETE:** a packet or a card missing a reading, or a unit not sent.\n   276\t  - This is a small design test, not release acceptance.\n   277\t\n   278\t## 5. What the result decides\n   279\t\n   280\t- **PASS:** judging-v13 earns a production design: automatic families in matching, lifecycle and the request builder, each a further\n   281\t  step Alex opens.\n   282\t- **STOP or INCOMPLETE:** the line goes back to Alex with the readings, and nothing is tuned on these 36 answers.\n   283\t\n   284\t## D753. The one-time v13s re-send (Alex: \"破例一次，付费重发\"), prepared before any answer exists\n   285\t\n   286\t- **The plan.** `paid-plan-v13s.json`, pinned `0dc7c310…` in `paid-plan-v13s.sha256`. It holds 12 requests × 3 draws = 36 first\n   287\t  attempts. Every request's system text is the registered D751 request (`080a0012…`). The cases are unchanged: three pairs, then O,\n   288\t  S (CY2027) and E.\n   289\t- **The cap.** $0.50 in total, diagnostic retries included (D732 and D753).\n   290\t- **Authorization.** One-time, at `~/.hivemind-keys/v13s-paid-gate/authorization.json`. The spent v13 authorization and the v13 pin\n   291\t  are unchanged. `send()` picks the pin and the authorization by the plan's format and refuses a mixed plan.\n   292\t- **Checked at $0,** with a stub gate and scratch key paths:\n   293\t  - an altered plan is refused, and so is a wrong ceiling;\n   294\t  - the pinned plan passes;\n   295\t  - a second use of the authorization is refused, and so is the spent v13 plan.\n   296\t- **Changes from council round 70** (`codex-r70.md`), made before the send. The verdict lines, the four questions and the\n   297\t  third-reader rule are unchanged.\n   298\t  1. **The card renderer** (`card_view`, `normalise`) now shows:\n   299\t     - every figure and passage the card's prose names, with the figures they rest on;\n   300\t     - a written range such as e5399–e5404 in full, with no width limit (council 70b);\n   301\t     - every passage in the card's `pushes` (council 70b: an unresolved E card had hidden 6 of the 15 passages it weighed). Figure ids inside the prose (reasons, why, basis_text) are\n   302\t     renumbered with the figures, so a prose reference points to the figure the writer meant.\n   303\t     - Checked at $0 on 20 stored v13s answers (D749–D751 and two controls): no dangling figure or passage reference, and every\n   304\t       shown value equal to the writer's.\n   305\t     - The re-check after council 70b covered every passage the answer names at card level (cites, pushes and prose, ranges\n   306\t       expanded). Missing: 0 of 20. Each unresolved card shows all 15 of its passages.\n   307\t  2. **The reader brief** is `reader-brief-v13s.md`. It is the v13 brief with Alex's two rulings, the same words for both readers and\n   308\t     the third reader:\n   309\t     - `usable` accepts an explained related figure (D747) and a \"can't tell yet\" that weighs the evidence, gives the target as\n   310\t       context and names the deciding fact (D753);\n   311\t     - `deciding_gap` is yes for a published number whose band an unsized adjustment determines, and no for a \"can't tell yet\".\n   312\t  3. **The exact file.** Readers receive the exact `packets.md` (`assemble_readings.py split-exact`; `third-exact` for the third\n   313\t     reader), with their packet ids named separately, so the sha256 the readings carry is the text they read.\n   314\t  4. **The launch.** It runs from the repository root, detached, with the log and pid outside the run folder:\n   315\t     `python3 docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py send poc/data/judging-v13s-paid-2026-11-23 0.5\n   316\t     docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.json`.\n   317\t     - All 36 scored attempts precede any diagnostic retry.\n   318\t     - A terminal transport failure on a first attempt makes the result INCOMPLETE.\n   319\t- **Re-checked after the changes:** rehearsal 19 of 19, paid mutants 33 of 33 with the control passing, cases 111 of 111, and the plan\n   320\t  pin unchanged.\nBLIND-RESULT.md\nBLIND2-RESULT.md\nBLIND3-RESULT.md\nBLIND4-RESULT.md\nBLIND5-RESULT.md\nBLIND6-RESULT.md\nBLIND7-RESULT.md\nDESIGN.md\nGATE-RESULT.md\nPAID-GATE-RESULT.md\nPAID-GATE.md\nPAPER-CHECK-D751.md\nREPAIR-DESIGN.md\nREQUEST-AUDIT.md\nRESULT.md\nSMALL-DESIGN.md\n__pycache__\nassemble_readings.py\nblind4.py\nblind5.py\nblind6.py\nblind7.py\nblind_adjudicate.py\nblind_reread.py\nblind_reread2.py\nblind_rules.py\nblind_test.py\ncalc_check.py\ncalc_small.py\nclaude-r45.md\nclaude-r48.md\nclaude-r49.md\nclaude-r56.md\nclaude-r57.md\nclaude-r58.md\nclaude-r59.md\nclaude-r61.md\nclaude-r63.md\nclaude-r65.md\nclaude-r67.md\ncodex-r45.md\ncodex-r45.stream\ncodex-r45b.md\ncodex-r45b.stream\ncodex-r46.md\ncodex-r46.stream\ncodex-r46aa.md\ncodex-r46aa.stream\ncodex-r46ab.md\ncodex-r46ab.stream\ncodex-r46ac.md\ncodex-r46ac.stream\ncodex-r46ad.md\ncodex-r46ad.stream\ncodex-r46b.md\ncodex-r46b.stream\ncodex-r46c.md\ncodex-r46c.stream\ncodex-r46d.md\ncodex-r46d.stream\ncodex-r46e.md\ncodex-r46e.stream\ncodex-r46f.md\ncodex-r46f.stream\ncodex-r46g.md\ncodex-r46g.stream\ncodex-r46h.md\ncodex-r46h.stream\ncodex-r46i.md\ncodex-r46i.stream\ncodex-r46j.md\ncodex-r4