{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **All 20 cards passed.** I rendered the 18 D749–D751 answers and the two controls through `card_lines`, using each answer’s own `item.json`. Every named passage appeared exactly as the writer saw it, and every figure reference in the prose resolved to the intended figure. All 208 displayed figures preserved the writer’s declared values, including all 61 in D751. The recomputed outcome is labeled separately. Each of the three unresolved E cards now shows all 15 passages it weighed. [E answer:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind7-2026-11-23/E/answers/codex.json:84) · [paid_gate.py:619](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:619)\n\n2. **Both fixes stay within round 70b’s request for the paid plan.** With citations and pushes cleared in memory, `e4687–e4764` alone displayed both endpoints and all three available passages between them. The push change also accepts `evidence` as a fallback spelling. The paid schema requires `evidence_id`, so that fallback has no effect on this launch. [paid_gate.py:496](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:496) · [paid_gate.py:579](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:579) · [render_v13.py:136](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:136)\n\n3. **The launch is ready.** The 12 rebuilt requests matched the pinned plan byte for byte (`0dc7c310…`). Three draws give 36 first attempts under the $0.50 total cap, including retries. I verified that the one-time authorization file and run folder were both absent. This review spent $0. [paid-plan-v13s.sha256:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan-v13s.sha256:1) · [PAID-GATE.md:286](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/PAID-GATE.md:286) · [paid_gate.py:431](/Users/lchingen/hiv